{
  "about": [
    "Every flag and subcommand Glasscode passes to `claude` and `codex`, by call site.",
    "script/cli-probe.sh checks each one against the CLIs' help: in CI against the help texts recorded in script/cli-help/ (one file per approved version), and by the owner against the real CLIs before a new version goes into cli-versions.json.",
    "A call site's `command` is the subcommand its flags follow (\"\" for none); the probe also checks that each word of it is a subcommand. `subcommands` are subcommands it passes after its flags.",
    "`help` names the help texts that --record records: the ones the call sites need.",
    "A known failure names a call site's id and one of its flags; the probe then warns instead of failing. Ids are unique.",
    "`--` (the end of the options) and the values of options are not probed. Change this file together with the call site."
  ],
  "help": {
    "claude": [""],
    "codex": ["", "exec", "resume", "login"]
  },
